Note that the maps with datapoints on them are [jittered]{.underline}, meaning that even if two species/data points are at the station and have the same lat/long coordinates, they may appear to be in slightly different positions. This is for ease of visualization, so that the points are not directly on top of each other, and all species at a given station can be viewed.

However, you will see if you hover over a datapoint, it displays the species, station name, and station number, so you can still identify which species were found at the same station.

